# Alembic

Bash into the container (```docker exec -it <container-name> /bin/bash```) and position yourself to the app folder. From here, you can run the following commands described in the next section.

## Commands

### Autogenerate migrations
Import the models you want to add in the backend/app/alembic/env.py file before running the autogenerate command.
```alembic revision --autogenerate -m "Description"```

### Apply migrations
```alembic upgrade head```

### Revert migrations
```alembic downgrade -X``` (X - number of migrations you want to go backwards)

### Check migration history
```alembic history```
